  m_Name: NacreSiltveilGrazer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  _stableId: nacre/species/siltveil-grazer
  _displayName: Siltveil Grazer
  _loreDescription: A low, broad-bodied grazer that sifts the pearlescent microbial mat spreading over disturbed Nacre soil through a soft fringe along its belly. A dorsal fan of thin plates folds flat against rock, so a resting grazer reads as another shell shard among the shards. It has no eyes to speak of; a ring of pressure pits around its snout reads footfalls through the ground, which is why it tracks movement rather than shapes and bolts at a sudden jolt from far beyond where a walking surveyor would register.
